# Enter splits a line at the cursor and Backspace at column 1 puts it back,
# which is the property that makes them a pair: the second undoes the first,
# and the cursor lands where the join is because that is where the person was
# looking. Delete at the end of a line is the same join from the other side.
#
# Enter arrives as carriage return and Backspace as ^H, which is what a
# terminal sends -- the editor takes 13, 10, 8 and 127 for the two of them.
name split.pas
size 8 20
push abcdef
push ghi
draw
esc C
esc C
esc C
ctrl M
draw
ctrl H
draw
esc F
esc 3~
draw
